"9244c46c-ed63-5ef5-b25d-ca51e142b429"] [:db/add "0faf9fd4-a04e-5eb0-991f-2443a2f7f221" :answer-field/correct "e67e530c-d28e-54f4-8748-5520d3b08f18"] [:db/ensure "0faf9fd4-a04e-5eb0-991f-2443a2f7f221" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/id #uuid "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3"] [:db/add "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{9 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/add "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{3 x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n9 x^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{3 x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{9 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"] [:db/add "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/answer-fields "0faf9fd4-a04e-5eb0-991f-2443a2f7f221"] [:db/ensure "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186064219 :knowledge-point/questions "0659bd20-fc90-57d9-99e5-b2b3ea9b8df3"] [:db/add "c7d761cd-609b-56d3-8734-276b3937faee" :answer/id #uuid "c7d761cd-609b-56d3-8734-276b3937faee"] [:db/add "c