-field/choices "3f03ac11-7a82-5c09-9079-684083d15035"] [:db/add "ce5c2999-7798-568b-92d7-f217b8df4f9b" :answer-field/choices "56d7db6e-245f-55e1-8d82-21fa80d199ba"] [:db/add "ce5c2999-7798-568b-92d7-f217b8df4f9b" :answer-field/choices "77593972-8883-57cf-8bf9-41d5bf9a74ec"] [:db/add "ce5c2999-7798-568b-92d7-f217b8df4f9b" :answer-field/choices "62b9cde0-3fb7-5728-9982-049c9e377fdc"] [:db/add "ce5c2999-7798-568b-92d7-f217b8df4f9b" :answer-field/correct "77593972-8883-57cf-8bf9-41d5bf9a74ec"] [:db/ensure "ce5c2999-7798-568b-92d7-f217b8df4f9b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf5" :question/id #uuid "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf5"] [:db/add "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf5" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{4 x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/add "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf5" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{2 x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n4 x^{2} + 9=9\\left(1+(\\frac{2 x}{3})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{4 x^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"] [:db/add "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "97955500-8434-5f88-8942-e141fc073cf